      "summary": "An agent run can be resumed after a restart without a tool acting twice. A tool's context carries `call: { id, round, attempt }` (the provider's tool-call id, the round, and how often this agent ran that id), so a tool with an effect keys it by the id; `onCheckpoint` on a send is called after each round's tool results with a copy of the messages, the steps, the round and the spend, the point a host persists and resumes from.",
      "id": "restartable-runs"
    },
